A||||5||Mr.Frosty||Will the intake manifold from a 3.4 pushrod work on a 2.8?||||1||
Z||000000||Mr.Frosty||05-04-2001||06:04 PM||||If it does,is there an advantage to it? If it does,will the throttle body from the 2.8 work on it too? Just wondering because I always hear that the intake from the 2.8 (upper and lower) bolts right onto it,but never hear about the reverse.Just trying to get ideas about intake options for my turbo,ya know,possible rerouting of the throttle body intake for more room.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top-ForSale <BR>85 GT Turbo-project car||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||05-04-2001||06:33 PM||||If the intake is from an aluminum head 3.4 pushrod (engine code E), it will not bolt up. AFAIK, the iron head 3.4 intake will.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||05-04-2001||06:36 PM||||The Fiero intake on the Iron 3.4 makes it look stock Fiero...that's the 'advantage'. Not even the Shadow knows it's not a 2.8||||reg||12
Z||000003||Cooter||05-04-2001||07:11 PM||||With 3.4 intake, the throttle body will be on the passenger side of the car and the drivers side of the intake will not clear the distributer. I had one cut and tig welded to provide enough room for the distributer, but then the water outlet became a problem, so I just stuck the Fiero intake back on.||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||05-04-2001||08:53 PM||||From looking at mine the bottom and middle intake manifolds are the same thing. The upper intake though is just shaped in a way so that a technician has access to the fuel injectors without having to remove the intake manifold. I think the fiero intake is better because it looks to have more volume. <P>Hey Cooter,<P>Why were you trying to adapt the 3.4 intake to your engine instead of using the 2.8 intake?<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||05-04-2001||10:17 PM||||Shorter runners, better top end flow.||||reg||1
